  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 234 PM EDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nModels are in good agreement that the mid-level low that has been \nparked over our CWA for the last few days will finally begin to \ndissolve as it shifts off toward the northeast through Wednesday. \nOur area will remain in a moist southwest flow along the periphery \nof a strengthening Bermuda high pressure. This will reinforce the \ncontinuation of a summertime pattern with decent PWATs ranging from \n1.5-2.0\" and diurnal thunderstorm chances each day through the \nperiod. The coverage of thunderstorms will be scattered to numerous \nthrough the period with plenty of instability over the region. In \naddition, ample afternoon cloud cover will suppress high \ntemperatures by a few degrees through Friday before higher heights \nbuild by late week, allowing for temperatures to climb into the \nupper 80s to low 90s as the high builds in closer to our area. While \nno organized severe weather is expected, a few storms may become \nstrong with gusty winds as the primary threat, in addition to \nlocalized flash flooding in areas with prolonged convective \nactivity.",
